#: ../../examples/notebooks/03_psf_and_pupils.ipynb:10002
msgid "3. Pupils and point-spread functions"
msgstr "3. Pupilles et fonctions d'étalement de point"

#: ../../examples/notebooks/03_psf_and_pupils.ipynb:10004
msgid "Telescope pupils are anti-aliased masks; the point-spread function (PSF) is the intensity in the focal plane. The PSF of a uniform circular pupil is the Airy pattern, with its first dark ring at $1.22\\,\\lambda/D$ (Born & Wolf, *Principles of Optics*, §8.5.2)."
msgstr "Les pupilles des télescopes sont des masques anticrénelés ; la fonction d'étalement de point (PSF) est l'intensité dans le plan focal. La PSF d'une pupille circulaire uniforme est la tache d'Airy, dont le premier anneau sombre est à $1.22\\,\\lambda/D$ (Born & Wolf, *Principles of Optics*, §8.5.2)."

